# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Working design notes, kept local
polyphony.md
retrain.md

# Job-hunt planning doc. Kept local: it is scaffolding for the repo's presentation,
# not part of the project, and it quotes numbers that are wrong until the fixes land.
better.md

# Kept local: the notebook that renders the preference chart. Its measurement code
# is utils/metric_utils.py, which IS tracked and is the part worth keeping — the
# notebook is the scratch around it, and carries ~144 KB of stored cell outputs.
preference_shift.ipynb

# Scratch renders, at ~450 KB each — preference_shift.ipynb still writes here. The
# tracked figures are figures/, which is what midi-gpt-post.md inlines; those are
# screenshots with no generator left in the repo, so do not delete them expecting a
# rebuild. The diagram sources that produced them were removed at 2026-08-26 and are
# recoverable from git history if a variant is ever needed again.
images/

# Generated MIDI
output/

# Experimental training runs. Weights must live OUTSIDE checkpoints/, not merely be
# ignored: latest_ckpt() globs CKPT_DIR and takes the highest ftN on disk, so an
# experimental checkpoint left there silently becomes the default for generation AND
# the policy start for the next DPO round. Pass --bass-ckpt / --ref-ckpt to use one.
#
# The .pt stay out. The *scripts* are tracked, because every published figure and
# number in the README is produced by one of them, and an untracked generator makes a
# figure an unreproducible screenshot. Measured JSON is tracked too — it is small, and
# it is the evidence behind the tables.
experiments/**
!experiments/**/
!experiments/**/*.py
!experiments/**/*.md
!experiments/**/*.json
experiments/**/*.pt

# Ableton analysis sidecars
*.asd

# Caches from the deleted audio-era pipeline. The directories no longer exist;
# the rules stay because stem_renders/ reappeared once after its rule was removed
# and 3.4 MB of it was committed before anyone noticed.
cache/
cond/
drum_cache/
drum_cond/
bass_cache/
bass_cond/
bass_grid/
bass_notes/
stems/
stem_renders/

# The source MIDI the .npz are mined from, vendored so mining is reproducible and every
# example can be traced back to a named pack file. Ignored for a stronger reason than the
# .npz below: these are the purchased pack files verbatim, not derivatives. The contents
# are excluded rather than the directory, so its README survives — git will not descend
# into an excluded directory to find a re-admitted file inside it.
training_data/corpus/*
!training_data/corpus/README.md

# Audio and arrays are ignored by default, then re-admitted below where the file
# is small, irreplaceable, or needed to run.
*.wav
*.npy
*.npz

# Tracked on purpose:
#   checkpoints/            the models. Not regenerable without retraining, and
#                           the training scripts only exist at 84f209b~1.
#   drum_samples/           the conditioning loops the pipeline needs to run.
#   training_data/dpo/      hand-edited MIDI — the only human-authored data here.
#
# NOT tracked: training_data/{bass,arp}_notes_midi/. Those 7,704 .npz are lossy but
# musically recognisable derivatives of purchased sample-pack MIDI — a clone could
# reconstruct the rhythm and intervals of 354 basslines from them. The licence covers
# using the packs, not redistributing derivatives, so they stay local and
# training_data/README.md records how to regenerate them.
!drum_samples/*.wav
!training_data/dpo/**/stems/
!training_data/dpo/**/stems/*.mid
!training_data/drum_loops/*.wav
.gstack/
